<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Euesperides</h1><p class="st-meta">600 BCE – 322 BCE (approx.) · capital Euesperides</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The westernmost Greek city of Cyrenaica, on the site of modern Benghazi, later refounded as Berenice.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Euesperides was founded on the shore of a lagoon near modern Benghazi, probably in the early 6th century BCE, by settlers from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-cyrene">Kingdom of Cyrene</a>. Its name recalls the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garden-of-the-hesperides">Garden of the Hesperides</a>, placed nearby by Greek legend. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arcesilaus-iv">Arcesilaus IV of Cyrene</a> sent new colonists there in the 460s BCE.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>It was a self-governing Greek city with a mixed farming and trading economy, producing grain and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olive-oil">olive oil</a> and exporting through its harbour. Excavations have found houses, pottery and coins. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thucydides">Thucydides</a> records that in 414 BCE the Spartan general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gylippus">Gylippus</a>, sailing to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syracuse">Syracuse</a>, helped the city lift a siege by Libyan tribes.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Euesperides passed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ptolemaic-empire">Ptolemaic Empire</a> in 322 BCE. In the mid-3rd century BCE its population moved to a new site, refounded as Berenice in honour of the wife of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemy-iii-euergetes">Ptolemy III</a>. Berenice later grew into the city of Benghazi.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 600 BCE – 322 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">city state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:47.76%;width:5.53%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>600 BCE – 322 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Euesperides</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ancient Greek religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Ancient Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/libya">Libya</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Hesperides, Berenice</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-461&amp;focus=euesperides" aria-label="Euesperides on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5197 1010 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Euesperides lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5517 1266L5772 1297"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5772 1297h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5517 1266h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5517 1266h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Euesperides. <a href="/atlas?year=-461&amp;focus=euesperides">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

